{"availability":"available","full":"calvinchengx/fabric-emulator","name":"fabric-emulator","description":"Local Microsoft Fabric emulator in one Go binary. Control plane, OneLake, T-SQL warehouse and Spark, verified against unmodified Microsoft tools.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":21,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-13T09:12:19Z","updated":"2026-10-07T00:40:52Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://calvinchengx.github.io/fabric-emulator/","topics":["azure","delta-lake","emulator","entra-id","golang","microsoft-fabric","onelake","spark","testing"],"demo":"https://calvinchengx.github.io/fabric-emulator/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:40.067Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:40.067Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:40.067Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:40.067Z","stars":21,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Coverage measures the unit suites. What catches consumer-facing defects is the e2e fleet, which no percentage scores — hence parity claims witnessed beside it: every claim of support names a test that exists and ran.","A clean-room, local emulator of Microsoft Fabric, built to compose with entra-emulator — the control plane (workspaces, items, RBAC, git, LROs, Fabric Core MCP) plus a real OneLake ADLS/Blob data plane, a T-SQL warehouse over TDS, native Livy sessions on a real Spark engine, Data Factory pipelines (Web, REST, Salesforce, and Azure Batch Custom on by default), Apache Airflow jobs on a real Airflow scheduler, KQL eventhouses, and Eventstream on a real Apache Kafka broker (Lakehouse and Reflex destinations included).","That is not a mock-up — it is the example below, filmed. Three source systems land, get conformed, resolve into one customer identity, and reach a Warehouse star that Power BI queries: PySpark on a real engine for bronze → silver, dbt-fabric over real TDS for gold. The run then publishes itself to OpenMetadata — domain, glossary, metrics, contracts and lineage, all derived from what it already knows rather than typed in twice. Every lineage edge records how it is known, so you can tell what the emulator watched from what a step merely claimed."],"features":["Test service-principal automation. SP → Fabric client-credentials against a","Deterministic long-running operations. Every Fabric mutation is async"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/calvinchengx/fabric-emulator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f6190f631c8853a6f755e56e35eeb5bd63b2775ef279d8059155fb8bf00e8ce6","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:40.227Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:40.227Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Coverage measures the unit suites. What catches consumer-facing defects is the e2e fleet, which no percentage scores — hence parity claims witnessed beside it: every claim of support names a test that exists and ran.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/calvinchengx/fabric-emulator/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f6190f631c8853a6f755e56e35eeb5bd63b2775ef279d8059155fb8bf00e8ce6","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/calvinchengx/fabric-emulator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:40.228Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T00:40:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/calvinchengx/fabric-emulator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:40.228Z","hash":"f6190f631c8853a6f755e56e35eeb5bd63b2775ef279d8059155fb8bf00e8ce6","originalBytes":22196,"storedBytes":22196,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["make","python","run","docker","real","docs","fabric","frozen","group","install","test","what","bash","capacities","coverage","data","e2e","emulator","every","one","rather","which","apache","built","local","only","over","warehouse","add","airflow","arm","behind","bronze","build","claims","clean","clean-room","colima","compose","conformed","consumer","container","containers","cu